+# Report Schema Contract: Threshold Support
+
+**Scope**: JSON and Markdown report format when thresholds are specified
+
+**Version**: 1.0
+
+## JSON Report Format
+
+### Without Thresholds (Backward Compatible)
+
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": {
+    "generatedAt": "2026-09-21T10:30:00Z",
+    "outputsPath": "/path/to/outputs.json",
+    "referencesPath": "/path/to/references.json",
+    "totalSamples": 100
+  },
+  "metrics": [
+    {
+      "id": "exact_match",
+      "score": 0.85,
+      "total": 100
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "f1",
+      "score": 0.88,
+      "total": 100
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### With Thresholds (New Fields)
+
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": {
+    "generatedAt": "2026-09-21T10:30:00Z",
+    "outputsPath": "/path/to/outputs.json",
+    "referencesPath": "/path/to/references.json",
+    "totalSamples": 100
+  },
+  "metrics": [
+    {
+      "id": "exact_match",
+      "score": 0.85,
+      "total": 100
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "f1",
+      "score": 0.88,
+      "total": 100
+    }
+  ],
+  "passed": false,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": 0.85,
+      "passed": false
+    },
+    {
+      "metric": "f1",
+      "min": 0.8,
+      "score": 0.88,
+      "passed": true
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### Schema Additions
+
+**New top-level field**: `passed` (boolean)
+- Required only when thresholds were specified
+- Absent when no thresholds used (backward compatible)
+- Value: `true` if all thresholds pass, `false` if any fail
+
+**New top-level field**: `thresholds` (array)
+- Required only when thresholds were specified
+- Absent when no thresholds used (backward compatible)
+- Array of threshold validation results; one per threshold in input
+
+**Threshold Object Structure**:
+```typescript
+{
+  metric: string,       // Metric identifier
+  min: number,          // Minimum threshold value (0-1)
+  score: number | null, // Actual metric score, null if absent
+  passed: boolean       // true if score !== null && score >= min
+}
+```
+
+### Field Validation Rules
+
+| Field | Type | Constraints |
+|-------|------|-------------|
+| `metric` | string | Matches metric id in `evaluations` or custom metric |
+| `min` | number | Range [0, 1], matches input threshold value |
+| `score` | number \| null | Range [0, 1] if number, null if metric has no score |
+| `passed` | boolean | Computed: `score !== null && score >= min` |
+
+## Markdown Report Format
+
+### Without Thresholds (Current)
+
+```markdown
+# Evaluation Report
+
+**Generated**: 2026-09-21T10:30:00Z
+**Outputs**: /path/to/outputs.json
+**References**: /path/to/references.json
+**Total Samples**: 100
+
+## Metrics
+
+| Metric | Score | Samples |
+|--------|-------|---------|
+| exact_match | 0.85 | 100 |
+| f1 | 0.88 | 100 |
+```
+
+### With Thresholds (New Section)
+
+```markdown
+# Evaluation Report
+
+**Generated**: 2026-09-21T10:30:00Z
+**Outputs**: /path/to/outputs.json
+**References**: /path/to/references.json
+**Total Samples**: 100
+
+## Metrics
+
+| Metric | Score | Samples |
+|--------|-------|---------|
+| exact_match | 0.85 | 100 |
+| f1 | 0.88 | 100 |
+
+## Thresholds
+
+| Metric | Min | Score | Status |
+|--------|-----|-------|--------|
+| exact_match | 0.90 | 0.85 | FAIL |
+| f1 | 0.80 | 0.88 | PASS |
+
+**Overall**: FAILED (1 of 2 thresholds failed)
+```
+
+### Threshold Section Rules
+
+**Header**: `## Thresholds` (h2 markdown)
+
+**Table Structure**:
+- Column 1: Metric name
+- Column 2: Min threshold value (formatted as decimal, e.g., "0.90")
+- Column 3: Score (formatted as decimal if number, "N/A" if null)
+- Column 4: Status ("PASS" or "FAIL" in uppercase)
+
+**Summary Line** (optional, after table):
+```markdown
+**Overall**: PASSED (all 2 thresholds passed)
+**Overall**: FAILED (1 of 2 thresholds failed)
+```
+
+### Backward Compatibility
+
+- Without thresholds: No "Thresholds" section added
+- Existing Markdown report consumers are unaffected
+
+## Example: Mixed Pass/Fail with Null Score
+
+### JSON
+```json
+{
+  "metadata": { ... },
+  "metrics": [
+    { "id": "exact_match", "score": null },
+    { "id": "f1", "score": 0.88 }
+  ],
+  "passed": false,
+  "thresholds": [
+    {
+      "metric": "exact_match",
+      "min": 0.9,
+      "score": null,
+      "passed": false
+    },
+    {
+      "metric": "f1",
+      "min": 0.8,
+      "score": 0.88,
+      "passed": true
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### Markdown
+```markdown
+## Thresholds
+
+| Metric | Min | Score | Status |
+|--------|-----|-------|--------|
+| exact_match | 0.90 | N/A | FAIL |
+| f1 | 0.80 | 0.88 | PASS |
+
+**Overall**: FAILED (1 of 2 thresholds failed)
+```
+
+## Number Formatting
+
+- **Scores and thresholds**: Formatted as decimals (e.g., "0.85", "0.9")
+- **Precision**: Match input precision; don't add trailing zeros
+- **Null scores in Markdown**: Display as "N/A" (not "null" or "undefined")
+
+## Notes for Implementers
+
+1. Only add `passed` and `thresholds` when thresholds were specified in input
+2. Maintain order of thresholds in output (same as input order)
+3. For Markdown, use standard markdown table syntax (pipes and dashes)
+4. Format numbers consistently (JSON uses JSON numbers; Markdown uses decimal strings)
+5. Summary line should state count of passed/failed thresholds clearly
